'''''Pandorea floribunda''''' is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Bignoniaceae]] and is [[endemic]] to eastern Australia. It is similar to ''[[Pandorea pandorana]]'' but the leaflets are egg-shaped, {{cvt|30–80|mm}} long and {{cvt|15–50|mm}} wide and the flowers are pale yellow to cream-coloured.<ref name="Guymer">{{cite journal |last1=Guymer |first1=Gordon P. |title=Two new species of Pandorea Spach (Bignoniaceae) recognised from Queensland |journal=Austrobaileya |date=2008 |volume=7 |issue=4 |page=736 |url=https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/281458#page/165/mode/1up |access-date=13 October 2021}}</ref> 

This species was first formally described in 1845 by [[Augustin Pyramus de Candolle]] who gave it the name ''Tecoma floribunda'' in his treatise, ''[[Prodromus Systematis Naturalis Regni Vegetabilis]]'' from an unpublished description by [[Allan Cunningham (botanist)|Allan Cunningham]].<ref name=APNI1>{{cite web|title=''Tecoma floribunda''|url= https://id.biodiversity.org.au/instance/apni/499935 |publisher=APNI|access-date=13 October 2021}}</ref><ref name="DC.">{{cite book |last1=de Candolle |first1=Augustin P. |title=Prodromus Systematis Naturalis Regni Vegetabilis |date=1845 |location=Paris |page=225 |url=https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/7158#page/230/mode/1up |access-date=13 October 2021}}</ref> In 2008, [[Gordon P. Guymer]] changed the name to ''Pandorea floribunda'' in the journal ''[[Austrobaileya (journal)|Austrobaileya]]''.<ref name=APNI>{{cite web|title=''Pandorea floribunda''|url= https://id.biodiversity.org.au/instance/apni/645456 |publisher=APNI|access-date=13 October 2021}}</ref><ref name="Black2">{{cite journal |last1=Black |first1=John McConnell |title=Additions to the Flora of South Australia. No. 35 |journal=Transactions and Proceedings of the Royal Society of South Australia |date=1927 |volume=61 |page=248 |url=https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/129822#page/292/mode/1up |access-date=13 October 2021}}</ref>

''Pandorea floribunda'' grows in forest, woodland and rainforest from sea level to an altitude of {{cvt|1200|m}} on the coast and ranges from [[Gladstone, Queensland|Gladstone]] in Queensland to [[Lismore, New South Wales|Lismore]] in New South Wales.<ref name="Guymer" />

